/* Ported verbatim from the production site (deeptech_frontend/src/content/data-processing-agreement.md). Do not edit wording here without legal review. */
const source: string = "# Data Processing Agreement - ASTEAI\n\n**Last Updated:** October 6, 2026 | **Version:** 1.0\n\n---\n\n## 1. Parties and Purpose\n\nThis Data Processing Agreement (\"DPA\") forms part of the agreement between **Startrit Infratech Pvt. Ltd.**, a company incorporated in India with its registered office in Chennai, Tamil Nadu, operating the ASTEAI platform (\"ASTEAI\", \"Processor\"), and the business customer that has accepted the ASTEAI Master Services Agreement, an Order Form, or the Terms and Conditions (\"Customer\", \"Controller\").\n\nIt applies whenever ASTEAI processes personal data **on the Customer's behalf** in providing the Services, for example candidate data that the Customer uploads to or collects through ASTEAI Hire (job applications, resumes, AI interview recordings, and assessment results).\n\nIt does not apply to personal data that ASTEAI processes for its own purposes as an independent controller or Data Fiduciary, such as the Customer's own user account details, billing records, or platform security logs. That processing is governed by the ASTEAI Privacy Policy.\n\nIf this DPA conflicts with the Master Services Agreement or the Terms and Conditions on the processing of Customer Personal Data, this DPA prevails.\n\n## 2. Definitions\n\n- **Applicable Data Protection Law:** The Digital Personal Data Protection Act, 2023 and its Rules (\"DPDP Act\"); the Information Technology Act, 2000 and rules under it; and, where they apply to the Customer, the EU General Data Protection Regulation (\"GDPR\"), the UK GDPR, and US state privacy laws.\n- **Customer Personal Data:** Personal data processed by ASTEAI on behalf of the Customer under this DPA, as described in Annex 1.\n- **Controller / Data Fiduciary** and **Processor / Data Processor** have the meanings given in the Applicable Data Protection Law. In this DPA the Customer is the Controller (Data Fiduciary) and ASTEAI is the Processor (Data Processor).\n- **Personal Data Breach:** A breach of security leading to accidental or unlawful destruction, loss, alteration, or unauthorised disclosure of, or access to, Customer Personal Data.\n- **Sub-processor:** A third party engaged by ASTEAI to process Customer Personal Data.\n\n## 3. Roles and Customer Instructions\n\n3.1 ASTEAI processes Customer Personal Data only on the Customer's documented instructions. The Agreement, the Customer's configuration of the Services, and the Customer's use of platform features (for example, inviting a candidate to an AI interview) are the Customer's complete instructions.\n\n3.2 ASTEAI will tell the Customer promptly if it believes an instruction infringes Applicable Data Protection Law, and may suspend that processing until the instruction is confirmed or changed.\n\n3.3 The Customer is responsible for:\n- having a lawful basis, including any required notice and consent, for the Customer Personal Data it provides or asks ASTEAI to collect;\n- the accuracy of that data;\n- the hiring and other decisions it makes. ASTEAI's AI scores, rankings, and recommendations support the Customer's decisions; they are not decisions in themselves. The Customer must ensure a human reviews any decision that significantly affects a candidate.\n\n## 4. Confidentiality\n\nASTEAI ensures that everyone authorised to process Customer Personal Data is bound by a duty of confidentiality and receives only the access needed for their role.\n\n## 5. Security\n\n5.1 ASTEAI implements the technical and organisational measures described in Annex 2. They are operated within an Information Security Management System certified to **ISO/IEC 27001:2022**.\n\n5.2 ASTEAI may update these measures, provided an update does not materially reduce the overall protection of Customer Personal Data.\n\n## 6. Sub-processors\n\n6.1 The Customer gives general authorisation for ASTEAI to engage the Sub-processors listed in Annex 3.\n\n6.2 ASTEAI will give the Customer at least **30 days' notice** by email or in-product notice before adding or replacing a Sub-processor. The Customer may object on reasonable data-protection grounds within that period. If the parties cannot resolve the objection, the Customer may terminate the affected Services and receive a pro-rata refund of prepaid fees for the unused period.\n\n6.3 ASTEAI imposes data-protection obligations on each Sub-processor that are no less protective than this DPA, and remains liable for its Sub-processors' performance.\n\n## 7. International Transfers\n\n7.1 Some Sub-processors process data outside India (see Annex 3). Transfers from India are made in accordance with Section 16 of the DPDP Act.\n\n7.2 Where the GDPR or UK GDPR applies to a transfer of Customer Personal Data to ASTEAI or its Sub-processors, the parties will rely on the European Commission's Standard Contractual Clauses (Module 2, controller to processor, or Module 3, processor to processor, as applicable), together with the UK International Data Transfer Addendum where relevant. These are incorporated by reference, with Annexes 1–3 of this DPA completing their appendices. The Customer may request a countersigned copy at compliance@asteai.com.\n\n## 8. Data Subject Requests\n\nASTEAI will, taking into account the nature of the processing, help the Customer respond to requests from individuals to exercise their rights (access, correction, erasure, grievance redressal, nomination, and others). If ASTEAI receives such a request directly, it will refer the individual to the Customer and will not respond itself except to confirm the referral, unless the law requires otherwise.\n\n## 9. Personal Data Breaches\n\n9.1 ASTEAI will notify the Customer **without undue delay, and in any event within 48 hours**, of becoming aware of a Personal Data Breach affecting Customer Personal Data.\n\n9.2 The notice will describe, as far as then known, the nature of the breach, the categories and approximate number of individuals and records affected, the likely consequences, and the measures taken or proposed. ASTEAI will provide further information as it becomes available.\n\n9.3 ASTEAI will cooperate with the Customer so that the Customer can meet its own notification obligations to the Data Protection Board of India, other supervisory authorities, and affected individuals. ASTEAI separately meets its own obligation to report cyber security incidents to CERT-In within 6 hours.\n\n## 10. Assistance and Audits\n\n10.1 ASTEAI will provide reasonable assistance with data protection impact assessments and prior consultations with authorities relating to the Services.\n\n10.2 ASTEAI will make available the information reasonably necessary to demonstrate compliance with this DPA, including its ISO/IEC 27001 certificate and responses to reasonable security questionnaires.\n\n10.3 If that information is not sufficient, or an authority requires it, the Customer may carry out an audit once in any 12-month period. The audit requires at least 30 days' written notice, must take place during business hours, and must be conducted at the Customer's cost by the Customer or an independent auditor bound by confidentiality. ASTEAI may charge reasonable costs for audits that go beyond this.\n\n## 11. Return and Deletion\n\n11.1 During the term, the Customer may export or delete Customer Personal Data through the Services or by request.\n\n11.2 Within **30 days** after the Services end, ASTEAI will delete Customer Personal Data, or return it first if the Customer asks within that period. Residual copies in encrypted backups are deleted in the normal backup cycle (no later than 90 days) and are not restored except for disaster recovery.\n\n11.3 ASTEAI may retain data where Indian or other applicable law requires it, and will keep any retained data confidential and process it only for that purpose.\n\n## 12. Liability and Term\n\n12.1 Each party's liability under this DPA is subject to the limitations and exclusions of liability in the Master Services Agreement or, if none is in place, the Terms and Conditions.\n\n12.2 This DPA continues for as long as ASTEAI processes Customer Personal Data.\n\n12.3 This DPA is governed by the law that governs the Master Services Agreement (or, if none, the Terms and Conditions), except where the Standard Contractual Clauses require otherwise.\n\n---\n\n## Annex 1 — Description of Processing\n\n| Item | Description |\n|------|-------------|\n| **Subject matter** | Provision of the ASTEAI Services to the Customer |\n| **Duration** | The term of the Agreement plus the deletion period in Section 11 |\n| **Nature and purpose** | Hosting, storing, and organising data; publishing job postings; collecting applications; conducting and recording AI-assisted interviews and assessments; transcribing audio; generating scores, summaries, and rankings; enabling communication between the Customer and candidates or experts; providing support |\n| **Categories of individuals** | Job applicants and candidates; the Customer's employees and authorised users; experts and contractors engaged through the platform |\n| **Categories of personal data** | Name, email address, phone number, location; resume/CV, education, employment history, skills; interview video and audio recordings and transcripts; assessment answers, code submissions, scores, and AI-generated evaluations; messages; usage data relating to the Services |\n| **Sensitive data** | Not intended. The Customer must not ask candidates for, or upload, financial account data, health data, biometric data, caste, religion, or similar information. ASTEAI does not extract biometric identifiers from recordings |\n| **Frequency** | Continuous, for the term |\n\n## Annex 2 — Technical and Organisational Measures\n\n1. **Governance:** ISO/IEC 27001:2022-certified ISMS, with an annual risk assessment, internal audit, and management review.\n2. **Access control:** Role-based access with least privilege; multi-factor authentication for administrative access; periodic access reviews; prompt removal of access when staff leave.\n3. **Encryption:** TLS 1.2 or higher in transit; AES-256 encryption at rest provided by our infrastructure providers.\n4. **Application security:** Code review before release; input validation; rate limiting; dependency vulnerability scanning; periodic penetration testing.\n5. **Logging and monitoring:** Authentication and administrative activity logging; application error monitoring with automated alerting.\n6. **Resilience:** Automated database backups with periodic restoration testing; business continuity plan reviewed annually.\n7. **Incident response:** Documented incident response procedure with defined roles, severity levels, CERT-In reporting, and post-incident review.\n8. **Supplier management:** Security review of Sub-processors before engagement, data processing terms with each, and annual review of critical suppliers.\n9. **People:** Confidentiality obligations for all staff and contractors; security and privacy awareness training.\n10. **Data minimisation:** Audio sent for transcription is discarded by the provider after transcription; AI prompts are limited to the data needed for the feature (see Privacy Policy Section 3.3).\n\n## Annex 3 — Authorised Sub-processors\n\n| Sub-processor | Purpose | Processing Location |\n|---------------|---------|---------------------|\n| Amazon Web Services (AWS) | Compute, storage, AI inference (Bedrock), translation, text-to-speech | India (Mumbai); Bedrock inference in the AWS region serving the request |\n| Supabase | Managed database, authentication, file storage | Australia (Sydney) |\n| Razorpay | Payment processing | India |\n| Groq | Speech-to-text transcription | United States |\n| Sentry | Error monitoring | United States |\n| PostHog | Product analytics | United States or EU |\n| Google LLC | Sign-in (Google One Tap) | United States |\n| Termly | Cookie consent management | United States |\n\nThis list matches Section 4.1 of the ASTEAI Privacy Policy. To subscribe to change notices, email compliance@asteai.com.\n\n---\n\n**Contact:** compliance@asteai.com · Startrit Infratech Pvt. Ltd., Chennai, Tamil Nadu, India - 600095\n";
export default source;
